course: dictionary
lesson: 4475
title: A spear with a hook
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things most children have never seen. You can often work out the meaning from the words around them. «Box jellyfish have tentacles covered in tiny stinging cells that fire like harpoons.» The word "like" is a clue: the cells fire the way something else fires, so a harpoon must be a thing that shoots out fast.
explain: A harpoon is a long spear with a sharp, hooked point, often tied to a rope. People use it to catch whales, big fish or seals. As a verb, to harpoon something means to hit or catch it with a harpoon. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The hunter speared the seal with a harpoon" still makes sense.
fact: A harpoon is a long spear with a sharp, hooked point, often tied to a rope.
fact: Harpoon can be a noun (a harpoon) or a verb (to harpoon something).
fact: Inuit hunters used harpoons to catch seals, and whaling ships used them to catch whales.
fact: Commercial whale hunting is now banned in most countries.
fact: «Harpoon gun» and «throw a harpoon» are phrases you may meet in history lessons.
exercise: What is a harpoon? | A type of hat worn by sailors | A small bird that sings at dawn | *A long spear with a sharp, hooked point, often tied to a rope
exercise: «The crew harpooned a large fish.» What does harpooned mean? | *Hit or caught with a harpoon | Painted in bright colours | Cooked over a fire
exercise: «Cone snails shoot a harpoon-like tooth full of venom into fish.» What does harpoon-like mean? | Covered in fur | *Shaped like or working like a harpoon | Soft and round like a ball | Very quiet and still
test: In «The whalers harpooned a whale», which part of speech is harpooned? | Noun | Adjective | Adverb | *Verb
test: «Old harpoon tips from the 1800s have been found in living whales.» Which clue tells you the tips are very old? | harpoon | *from the 1800s | living whales | found
exam: «Box jellyfish have tentacles covered in tiny stinging cells that fire like harpoons.» What does "like harpoons" tell you about how the cells work? | They change colour | They float slowly in the water | *They shoot out quickly, like a spear | They make a sound
